<!--
  Adaptive-icon foreground: white fish facing left.

  Everything stays inside the 66dp safe circle (centre 54,54 / radius 33) so round and
  squircle launcher masks never clip the tail: the widest points are the tail tips at
  (77.5, 38) and (77.5, 70), i.e. radius 30.5. The white mass is centred by centroid,
  not by bounding box, because the tail is a light shape and the body is heavy.

  The gill is a hole in the silhouette (evenOdd subpath) rather than a stroke: a white
  stroke on a white body is invisible, and a hole follows whatever the launcher shows
  behind the icon instead of hardcoding the background colour.
-->
